d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","headline":"\u00a354k Scottish Welfare Fund overspend requiring drawdown from earmarked reserves","detail":"The Scottish Welfare Fund (part of a wider \u00a374k Benefits & Money Advice overspend) has exceeded budget by \u00a354k due to higher activity levels. The council will cover this from earmarked reserves, showing service demand growth outpacing budgeted provision.","category":"reserves","matters":"Reserve drawdown signals welfare spending is unsustainable at budgeted levels; demonstrates service demand exceeding policy expectations.","figures":"\u00a354k Scottish Welfare Fund overspend met from reserves","quote":"There is an overall overspend of \u00a374k, predominantly arising from an overspend of \u00a354k in the Scottish Welfare Fund due to higher activity levels, but which will subsequently be met from a balance of earmarked reserves.","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-10","committee":"10 September 2026","paper_title":"Housing, Property and Communities Budget Monitoring Report to 30 June 2026","paper_url":"https://moray.cmis.uk.com/Moray/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=Y31%2bEQrmqkvk3HB2F3v3NMEL59yMsF3ddcr5oyJWncDhgUb31KE4XQ%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","headline":"Housing Benefits budget structurally underfunded, creating baseline overspends","detail":"Housing Benefits shows a \u00a315k Q1 overspend. The council explicitly states this \"arises from a historically low budget provision which is subject to review\"\u2014acknowledging the budget was never set at a sustainable level for actual demand.","category":"overspend","matters":"This is not a one-off variance but a structural mismatch between service demand and budget; signals ongoing pressure that cannot be managed within current provision.","figures":"\u00a315k Housing Benefits overspend from historically low budget","quote":"An overspend of \u00a315k in Housing Benefits arises from a historically low budget provision which is subject to review","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-10","committee":"10 September 2026","paper_title":"Housing, Property and Communities Budget Monitoring Report to 30 June 2026","paper_url":"https://moray.cmis.uk.com/Moray/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=Y31%2bEQrmqkvk3HB2F3v3NMEL59yMsF3ddcr5oyJWncDhgUb31KE4XQ%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","headline":"\u00a31,277k savings target includes \u00a3926k from capitalising PFI lifecycle costs, not operational savings","detail":"Only \u00a375k of \u00a31,277k proposed savings have been delivered by end Q1. The largest single item is \u00a3926k from capitalising PFI lifecycle costs\u2014an accounting reclassification, not real expenditure reduction. Another \u00a31,059k is expected in Q2, with \u00a3143k still under review to confirm whether already \"baselined\" into existing budgets.","category":"savings","matters":"Real operational savings and accounting treatments are not equivalent; relying on capitalisation to balance budgets signals potential structural underfunding; actual delivery rate is 6% to date.","figures":"\u00a31,277k proposed savings, \u00a375k posted, \u00a3926k capitalising PPP lifecycle costs, \u00a31,059k expected Q2, \u00a3143k under review","quote":"Work on the proposed savings for Elgin Community Centre (\u00a340k), Homelessness/allocations recharges from resettlement (\u00a325k), Capitalising PPP lifecycle costs (\u00a3926k) and Smarter Working (\u00a368k) remains ongoing, with the majority expected to be posted in the course of Quarter 2","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-10","committee":"10 September 2026","paper_title":"Housing, Property and Communities Budget Monitoring Report to 30 June 2026","paper_url":"https://moray.cmis.uk.com/Moray/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=Y31%2bEQrmqkvk3HB2F3v3NMEL59yMsF3ddcr5oyJWncDhgUb31KE4XQ%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","headline":"\u00a3191k HRA rental income loss from EPC discount delays in housing improvement programme","detail":"House rents are \u00a3191k below budget in Q1 because more tenancies are retaining an Energy Performance Certificate discount pending completion of energy efficiency works on their properties. The council notes progress is being reviewed in Q2, meaning the works are behind schedule.","category":"income","matters":"HRA is self-financing through rents; delays in capital works create income volatility and signal the housing improvement programme may be running behind schedule.","figures":"\